      {
        "id": "the-expensive-mistake-is-ignoring-the-light",
        "title": "The expensive mistake is ignoring the light",
        "description": "“The light came on but the gauge is fine - I'll keep driving.”",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The coolant light is a warning. The gauge is the confirmation. Don't ignore the light."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“I'll just top up the coolant when I get home.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Coolant loss while driving can lead to rapid overheating. Stop and check."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“Opening the coolant reservoir is fine when hot.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "NEVER open the coolant reservoir when hot. Pressurised coolant causes severe burns."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“I'll just use water - it's fine.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Water isn't coolant. It boils at a lower temperature and lacks corrosion inhibitors. Use proper coolant."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“The light came on once and went off - it's fine.”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Intermittent lights indicate intermittent problems. The fault is still there."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Diagnostic flowchart"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-expensive-mistake-is-ignoring-the-light",
          "order": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "follow-this-decision-tree-to-identify-the-cause",
        "title": "Follow this decision tree to identify the cause",
        "description": "COOLANT WARNING LIGHT │ ├─── Which light is on? │ │ │ ├── RED thermometer → STOP ENGINE → Emergency │ │ │ └── YELLOW waves (coolant level) → Check coolant (cold) │ ├─── Check coolant level (engine COLD) │ │ │ ├── Normal → Sensor or wiring → Coolant sensor │ │ │ └── Low → Top up and monitor → Coolant leak │ ├─── Any other symptoms? │ │ │ ├── White smoke → Head gasket → Head gasket │ │ │ ├── Puddle under car → External leak → Coolant leak │ │ │ ├── Heater not working → Air in system → Air lock │ │ │ └── No other symptoms → Monitor │ └─── Professional diagnostic (£50-£150) │ ├── Pressure test → Find external leaks │ ├── Exhaust gas test → Check for head gasket │ └── Thermostat check → Check if stuck",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Coolant warning light types & repair costs"
          }
        ],
