      {
        "id": "identify-check-diagnose",
        "title": "Identify, check, diagnose",
        "description": null,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Step 1: Identify which light is on Red thermometer? → STOP DRIVING Yellow/red waves? → Check coolant level (when cold)",
              "Step 2: Check coolant level (when cold) Wait 30+ minutes after driving · Open the coolant reservoir slowly (cover with a cloth) · Is the level between min and max?",
              "Step 3: If coolant level is low Top up to the correct level · Use the correct coolant type for your vehicle · Monitor for future loss",
              "Step 4: If coolant level drops again Book a diagnostic (£50-£150) - there is a leak in the system",
              "Step 5: Professional diagnostic (£50-£150) A technician will pressure test the cooling system, check for exhaust gases in coolant (head gasket test), inspect for external leaks, and test thermostat and water pump function."
